.TH invaders 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
invaders \- Space Invaders drawn in text characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B invaders
.SH DESCRIPTION
Thomas Munro's ascii invaders: rows of aliens built out of letters and
punctuation march across the screen and down towards you, dropping
bombs, while you shoot back from behind a row of shelters.  A mothership
crosses the top now and then for a mystery score.
.PP
The screen must be at least 80 columns by 20 lines; the console is 80 by
40.  It is drawn with
.BR curses ,
so
.B TERM
has to name an entry in
.BR /etc/termcap .
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B space
Start a game from the title screen, and fire.
.TP
.BR j " or left arrow"
Move left.
.TP
.BR k " or right arrow"
Move right.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
The aliens are worth 10, 20 and 30 points by row.  You start with three
lives in reserve.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR startrek (1),
.BR 2048 (1)
